From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:22:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: spoof Chrome MemoryInfo with native coarse snapshots

Expose Performance.prototype.memory only in Window realms and return a fresh
native MemoryInfo wrapper per read. Implement all three enumerable read-only
prototype getters with coherent fixed bucketed values: totalJSHeapSize and
usedJSHeapSize are 10,000,000 bytes; jsHeapSizeLimit is 3,760,000,000 bytes.

Keep the base MacBook Neo / A18 Pro / 8GB RAM / 256GB SSD persona. These are
spoofed Chrome coarse readings, not measurements from a Neo, host RAM,
container memory or the actual V8 heap. Chrome's precise-versus-bucketed mode
depends on process site-locking; no site-lock/precise/live-usage simulation is
introduced here. Leave StorageManager's quota and the real V8 cap unchanged.

Add opt-in LegacyNoInterfaceObject metadata to snapshot installation: retain
the native template and MemoryInfo brand, omit the global interface and its
prototype's own constructor. Other interfaces keep their existing behavior.
Use the Performance receiver wrapper's realm and weak RC finalization so
fresh snapshots are collectible and held snapshots survive GC/frame removal.

Current Chromium IDL/source plus native Chrome 154 diagnostics confirm the
shape: fresh wrappers, inherited Object constructor, brand/descriptors,
native illegal-receiver errors and receiver-realm behavior. The page persona
remains the existing Chrome 155; the fixed values are an observed coarse
Chrome profile, not a pinned macOS-specific precise limit.

References:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/memory_info.idl
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/window_performance.cc
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/memory_info.cc

Validation: release build, 1658 existing upstream tests, and 44 temporary
native-shape/realm/worker/isolated-world/navigation/GC checks pass. Diagnostics
use iframe/worker resource loading and expose-gc only for coverage; benchmark
validation uses the standard server command. No new tests or benchmark edits.
---
 src/browser/js/Snapshot.zig        | 12 +++++-
 src/browser/webapi/Performance.zig | 63 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/browser/js/Snapshot.zig b/src/browser/js/Snapshot.zig
index 220496e..8a471c7 100644
--- a/src/browser/js/Snapshot.zig
+++ b/src/browser/js/Snapshot.zig
@@ -326,7 +326,8 @@ fn createSnapshotContext(
         @setEvalBranchQuota(10_000);
         const template_index = comptime bridge.JsApiLookup.getId(JsApi);
         const func = v8.v8__FunctionTemplate__GetFunction(templates[template_index], context);
-        if (@hasDecl(JsApi.Meta, "name")) {
+        const no_interface_object = comptime @hasDecl(JsApi.Meta, "no_interface_object") and JsApi.Meta.no_interface_object;
+        if (@hasDecl(JsApi.Meta, "name") and !no_interface_object) {
             const name = JsApi.Meta.name;
             const v8_class_name = v8.v8__String__NewFromUtf8(isolate, name.ptr, v8.kNormal, @intCast(name.len));
             var maybe_result: v8.MaybeBool = undefined;
@@ -342,6 +343,15 @@ fn createSnapshotContext(
             }
         }
 
+        if (no_interface_object) {
+            // [LegacyNoInterfaceObject] also omits prototype.constructor.
+            const proto = v8.v8__Object__Get(@ptrCast(func), context, prototype_key) orelse return error.PrototypeLookupFailed;
+            const constructor_key = v8.v8__String__NewFromUtf8(isolate, "constructor", v8.kNormal, 11);
+            var result: v8.MaybeBool = undefined;
+            v8.v8__Object__Delete(@ptrCast(proto), context, constructor_key, &result);
+            if (!result.has_value or !result.value) return error.ConstructorDeleteFailed;
+        }
+
         if (comptime @hasDecl(JsApi.Meta, "array_iterator") and JsApi.Meta.array_iterator) {
             // Use the realm's intrinsic, not a custom callback or injected JS.
             const array = v8.v8__Array__New(isolate, 0).?;
